1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:16,550
All five stories from lessons 11–15 — four pictures each and a full model story in the past tense. Plus twelve phrases that work for any story and five mistakes that cost people points. Get ready and tell the stories out loud!

2
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:28,634
How does task 3 work? You get four pictures that together tell one story. You tell what happened — in the past tense. You can get ten points for this task.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:53,482
The most important thing is the past tense. Man: šel, měl, byl. Woman: šla, měla, byla. Several people: šli, měli, byli. And when you talk about yourself, don’t forget jsem: šel jsem, šla jsem. Now we go through all five stories. First tell it yourself, then you hear the model.

4
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:57,652
Story 11: An accident in the car park.

5
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:00,017
What happened to Mrs Novotná yesterday?

6
00:01:12,667 --> 00:01:15,633
Yesterday afternoon Mrs Novotná drove to the shops.

7
00:01:15,833 --> 00:01:18,067
She arrived at the supermarket car park.

8
00:01:18,267 --> 00:01:21,933
Later, when she was reversing, she didn't see another car and hit it.

9
00:01:22,133 --> 00:01:24,067
The car had a broken light.

10
00:01:24,267 --> 00:01:27,700
Mrs Novotná was frightened, but nobody was hurt.

11
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:30,000
The owner of the other car was angry.

12
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,200
Mrs Novotná called the police.

13
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:35,567
The police arrived twenty minutes later and checked the documents.

14
00:01:35,767 --> 00:01:41,033
In the end Mrs Novotná and the other driver filled in an insurance form and went home.

15
00:01:41,233 --> 00:01:43,817
Story 12: The ambulance.

16
00:01:44,567 --> 00:01:46,106
What happened to Grandma yesterday?

17
00:01:58,767 --> 00:02:01,700
Yesterday morning Grandma was at home cooking lunch.

18
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:04,733
The kitchen floor was wet and Grandma fell.

19
00:02:04,933 --> 00:02:07,200
Her leg hurt and she couldn't get up.

20
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,100
Luckily her grandson was at home.

21
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:13,933
He immediately called 155 and said what had happened and where they live.

22
00:02:14,133 --> 00:02:16,067
The ambulance arrived ten minutes later.

23
00:02:16,267 --> 00:02:18,767
The paramedics took Grandma to hospital.

24
00:02:18,967 --> 00:02:21,933
At the hospital the doctor examined her and did an X-ray.

25
00:02:22,133 --> 00:02:24,633
Her leg wasn't broken, only bruised.

26
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:26,700
In the evening Grandma could go home.

27
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:29,484
Story 13: A new flat.

28
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:32,243
What did Ivan and Olena do last week?

29
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:47,633
Last week Ivan and Olena were looking for a new flat.

30
00:02:47,833 --> 00:02:51,067
In the evening they sat at the computer and searched for a flat online.

31
00:02:51,267 --> 00:02:53,300
They found a nice flat near the centre.

32
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,367
Then they went to a viewing.

33
00:02:55,567 --> 00:02:58,933
The owner showed them the kitchen, the bedroom and the balcony.

34
00:02:59,133 --> 00:03:02,433
They really liked the flat because it was bright and clean.

35
00:03:02,633 --> 00:03:04,967
The next day they signed the rental contract.

36
00:03:05,167 --> 00:03:07,400
They paid the deposit and the first rent.

37
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:09,700
Finally they got the keys from the owner.

38
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:12,867
They were very happy because they finally had a place of their own.

39
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:16,121
Story 14: The Czech exam.

40
00:03:16,867 --> 00:03:18,510
What did Oksana do last month?

41
00:03:31,167 --> 00:03:33,933
Last month Oksana took a Czech exam.

42
00:03:34,133 --> 00:03:36,067
Every evening she studied Czech.

43
00:03:36,267 --> 00:03:39,733
She read texts, listened to recordings and wrote e-mails.

44
00:03:39,933 --> 00:03:42,633
On Saturday morning she went to the exam at a language school.

45
00:03:42,833 --> 00:03:44,467
She was a bit nervous.

46
00:03:44,667 --> 00:03:48,433
First she did the written test: reading, writing and listening.

47
00:03:48,633 --> 00:03:51,033
The test was hard, but she managed it.

48
00:03:51,233 --> 00:03:54,333
A month later she got a certificate that she had passed.

49
00:03:54,533 --> 00:03:57,300
She was very happy and called her husband straight away.

50
00:03:57,500 --> 00:04:00,100
In the evening she celebrated with her family at a restaurant.

51
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:03,354
Story 15: Fixing the bike.

52
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:06,240
What did Matvij do with his dad on Saturday?

53
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:22,933
On Saturday Matvij wanted to ride his bike, but it had a flat tyre.

54
00:04:23,133 --> 00:04:25,233
He was sad because he couldn't ride.

55
00:04:25,433 --> 00:04:26,833
He told his dad.

56
00:04:27,033 --> 00:04:30,933
Dad and Matvij went to a sports shop.

57
00:04:31,133 --> 00:04:33,533
There they bought a new inner tube and a pump.

58
00:04:33,733 --> 00:04:36,233
Then they fixed the bike together in front of the house.

59
00:04:36,433 --> 00:04:39,667
Dad changed the inner tube and Matvij pumped up the tyre.

60
00:04:39,867 --> 00:04:41,767
Finally the bike was fine.

61
00:04:41,967 --> 00:04:43,967
Matvij rode his bike down the street.

62
00:04:44,167 --> 00:04:46,567
He was very happy and thanked his dad.

63
00:04:46,767 --> 00:04:52,093
Now twelve phrases that work for any story. Listen and repeat out loud.

64
00:04:53,233 --> 00:04:55,060
Yesterday morning I got up at seven.

65
00:04:58,700 --> 00:05:00,030
First I had breakfast.

66
00:05:03,667 --> 00:05:05,284
Then I went to work.

67
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:10,551
Suddenly it started to rain.

68
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:15,504
In the end we went home.

69
00:05:19,167 --> 00:05:21,411
He was tired because he worked a lot.

70
00:05:25,067 --> 00:05:27,206
They had no umbrella, so they were wet.

71
00:05:30,867 --> 00:05:32,171
The weather was nice.

72
00:05:35,833 --> 00:05:37,451
In the afternoon she went to the police.

73
00:05:41,100 --> 00:05:42,534
Marie had a birthday.

74
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,739
Mr Tichý had to stay at home.

75
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:53,148
In the evening friends came.

76
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:59,645
Five typical mistakes that cost people points.

77
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:10,717
Correct: Olga ležela v posteli. Tell the story in the past tense: ležela, šla, koupila.

78
00:06:14,867 --> 00:06:25,418
Correct: Marie pekla dort. Woman: -la. Man: -l. Several people: -li.

79
00:06:29,567 --> 00:06:35,625
Correct: Včera jsem šel do práce. When you talk about yourself, don’t forget jsem.

80
00:06:39,767 --> 00:06:51,363
Correct: Ráno balili věci a potom přijelo auto. Don’t describe the pictures. Tell a story with linking words: nejdřív, potom, nakonec.

81
00:06:55,500 --> 00:07:06,103
Correct: Jel na kole do práce. Najednou vyběhl pes a on spadl. Say two or three sentences for each picture: who, where, what and why.

82
00:07:07,767 --> 00:07:27,121
Summary. First: tell the story in the past tense. Second: link your sentences — nejdřív, potom, nakonec. Third: two or three sentences for each picture. And fourth: watch the gender — on šel, ona šla.

83
00:07:28,767 --> 00:07:40,128
Which story is the hardest for you? Write it in the comments — and try writing the first two sentences in the past tense there. And if the video helps you, subscribe — there's a new video every day.

84
00:07:41,767 --> 00:07:58,065
On the Zkouška A2 nanečisto website you can practise all stories for free — it listens and checks your past tense. Link in the description. Tomorrow: big review of Speaking task 4. Subscribe so you don’t miss anything.
